1
00:00:00,478 --> 00:00:04,522
A request changes launch scope. Who makes sure the spec catches up?

2
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:10,059
Orchestra gives product teams a queue for changes that need a decision.

3
00:00:10,289 --> 00:00:13,264
Here, the team has asked to add PDF export.

4
00:00:14,409 --> 00:00:18,270
The change packet puts the previous wording beside the request.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,591
The evidence stays attached, so the reviewer can see where it came from.

6
00:00:23,477 --> 00:00:25,823
An authorized reviewer makes the call.

7
00:00:26,053 --> 00:00:29,523
Now there’s a recorded decision, not just a request.

8
00:00:30,486 --> 00:00:33,761
Project Memory shows what the decision connects to.

9
00:00:33,991 --> 00:00:38,514
Follow the branch to the underlying document, right down to the passage.

10
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:43,723
With Socrates, a question about the spec gets a cited answer.

11
00:00:43,953 --> 00:00:47,068
Open the source to check exactly what the spec says.

12
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:54,145
Use Agent Preflight to package the approved context for your coding agent.

13
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:58,776
Orchestra. Product Brain for High Speed Teams.
